// Selective member import (`use std.<mod>.<fn>`) brings a module function into scope under its bare
// name, callable without the `module.` qualifier. The braced group form imports several at once, and
// a single name needs no braces. Dispatched through the same `call_native_module` path as the
// qualified call, so both backends agree by construction (prelude-redesign P0).
// expect: stdout "4.0"
// expect: stdout "5"
// expect: stdout "9"
// expect: stdout "3"
// expect: stdout "5.0"
// expect: exit 0
use std.math.sqrt
use std.math.{abs, max}
use std.{math}

echo sqrt(16.0)
echo abs(-5)
echo max(3, 9)
// The qualified form still works alongside a selective import of the same module.
echo math.floor(3.7)
// A selectively-imported function is a first-class value — bind it, then call through the binding.
f = sqrt
echo f(25.0)
